# Umbra Nemotron assistant (NVIDIA Nemotron through Nebius Token Factory).
# Used by the local Vite server (npm run dev / npm run preview). Vite does not load these
# from .env files for the server: export them in your shell before starting it.
# Never put the API key itself in this file or in any VITE_ variable.

# 1 turns the assistant on. Anything else keeps it off and nothing is sent anywhere.
NEMOTRON_ENABLED=
# Spending cap in US dollars, shared by every local server using the same usage log and kept
# across restarts. Empty or 0 keeps the assistant off.
NEMOTRON_BUDGET_USD=
# Path to a file holding only the Token Factory API key (absolute, so every checkout finds the same file). Its
# name must end in .key, and it must be a regular file you own, chmod 600, not a symlink and with no other hard
# links. Keep it outside the project folder or under .local/ (for example .local/secrets/). The dev server never
# serves .local/ or *.key files and refuses any key file it could serve.
TOKEN_FACTORY_KEY_FILE=
# JSON-lines spending log. Default: nemotron-usage.jsonl in the key file's folder (symlinks resolved), so every
# checkout or worktree using the same key file shares one cap. If set, it must be an absolute path.
NEMOTRON_USAGE_LOG=
# The local route answers only requests to localhost, 127.0.0.1 or [::1] from this machine.

# Hosted Sites worker: Nemotron is off in code until a durable shared budget exists and hosted
# use is authorized. Host variables cannot turn it on.
